index 0000000..3ee411a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,111 @@
+# U2AC web UI
+
+A status and settings page for the dongle: one static `index.html` (inline CSS/JS, no external
+resources, about 32 KB) plus POSIX `sh` CGI scripts that use BusyBox applets only. BusyBox `httpd`
+serves it; nothing else is needed.
+
+## Starting it
+
+```sh
+httpd -p 10.0.0.1:80 -h /usr/share/u2ac/www        # on the AP, after `ip addr add 10.0.0.1/24 dev wlan0`
+httpd -p 192.168.50.2:80 -h /usr/share/u2ac/www    # on the USB (NCM) link, once usb0 has its address
+```
+
+`u2ac-aa` starts both: the AP instance in `ap_up`, the USB one there or, when NCM comes up later (the boot's
+USB probe delays it, a late computer gets it after the AP), as soon as a computer is found (`usb_httpd`).
+
+- Run it as root: the CGIs write `/run/persist`, call `btmgmt`, `u2ac-aa`, `persist` and `reboot`.
+- `httpd` can bind only to an address that already exists, so start each instance after its address is up.
+- aa-proxy-rs's own web server listens on `127.0.0.1:8080` only (shipped config.toml: no login, settings
+  that run shell commands), so it never clashes with this one on :80. Reach it over ssh:
+  `ssh -L 8080:127.0.0.1:8080 root@10.0.0.1`, then http://localhost:8080.
+- Files: `cgi-bin/*` must be mode 0755, `cgi-bin/_lib.sh` mode 0644 (sourced, never run; `httpd` answers
+  404 for it).
+
+## Endpoints
+
+Every CGI prints `Content-Type: application/json` and a JSON object with `"ok"`. Failures are
+`{"ok":false,"error":"<text>","code":"<code>"}` with HTTP 200.
+
+| Endpoint | Method | What it returns or does |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cgi-bin/status` | GET | Dashboard object (polled every 3 s): `aa.state` (`off`, `waiting`, `connected`, `streaming`), `aa.last` (newest aa-proxy-rs log line), `mode.set` (`auto`, `dev`, `aa`) and `mode.active` (`aa`, `maint`), `svc.*` daemon booleans, `wifi` (ssid, channel, freq, width, txpower, `clients[]` with signal dBm, tx/rx bitrate, connected time, DHCP ip/host), `bt` (addr, name, powered, discoverable, paired count), `sys` (uptime, load, CPU kHz/max/governor, memory, `temp_mc` or null, build, kernel). |
+| `cgi-bin/logs?src=S&n=N` | GET | Last N lines (20 to 500, default 200), ANSI codes stripped. S: `aa` (`/var/log/aa-proxy-rs.log`, falls back to `/run/log/aa-proxy-rs.console`), `svc` (`/run/log/u2ac-aa.log`), `hostapd`, `bt` (`/run/log/bluetoothd.log`), `web` (`/run/log/u2ac-web.log`, this UI's own change log), `dmesg`, `flight` (the flight recorder: its list, then the newest car run from its top, `u2ac-aa flightlog`). |
+| `cgi-bin/settings` | GET | Wi-Fi name (override, else config.toml, else hostapd.conf), the SSID the AP runs now, `wifi.width` (`set` 40 or 80, `live` MHz now, `vht80`: the firmware offers 80 MHz on channel 36), `opts` (every `opt` key's current value), Bluetooth name, paired devices (`/var/lib/bluetooth/<adapter>/<device>/info`), startup mode, `pending_reboot`, whether `reboot-recovery` exists, `home` (home upload: `set`, `ssid`, `url`, `last` = this boot's outcome). Never a password or key. |
+| `cgi-bin/about` | GET | Versions (kernel, build, board, aa-proxy-rs, BlueZ, hostapd, iw, BusyBox; cached for the boot in `/run/u2ac-web/versions`) and cpufreq `time_in_state`. |
+| `cgi-bin/token` | GET | The access code, when this request may see it (see Security). |
+| `cgi-bin/action` | POST | Changes. Form-urlencoded body: `token=<code>&confirm=yes&action=<a>` plus fields below. |
+
+`action` values:
+
+| action | Fields | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| `wifi` | `ssid`, `psk`, `alias` (each optional, empty keeps the current value) | Rewrites the first `  ssid = "…"`, `  wpa_passphrase = "…"` and `  btalias = "…"` lines of `/etc/aa-proxy-rs/config.toml`, writes `/run/persist/u2ac-wifi.conf`, then `u2ac-aa persist`. Applies after a reboot. |
+| `forget` | `dev=AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF` or `dev=all` | `btmgmt -i hci0 unpair`, removes the device directory (and its `cache/` entry), then `u2ac-aa persist`. |
+| `mode` | `to=auto`, `maintenance` or `aa` | `u2ac-aa dev off`, `dev on` or `dev aa` (from the next boot). |
+| `opt` | `key`, `value` (only these pairs) | `guard` on/off (hands-free guard, flag `u2ac-hfp-guard-off`), `flightlog` on/off (`u2ac-flightlog-off`, at once), `sleep` on/off (car-off sleep, `u2ac-sleep-off`, at once), `fastflash` on/off (NOR at 49.5 MHz during the boot, `u2ac-qspi-normal`), `led` on/off (`u2ac-led-off`, at once), `btbaud` fast/slow (`u2ac-bt-slowbaud`), `btpatch` stock/0092 (`u2ac-bt-0092`), `usbchunk` 512/1024/2048/4096/8192/16384 (`u2ac-ffs-chunk`, 16384 = default = no file). Then `u2ac-aa persist`. |
+| `width` | `to=40` or `80` | Creates or removes `/run/persist/u2ac-wifi-80`, then `u2ac-aa persist`. The hotspot runs at 80 MHz from the next boot only when the firmware offers VHT80 on channel 36. 40 MHz is the default. |
+| `home` | `ssid`, `psk`, `url` (`psk` may stay empty when the name is unchanged) | Home upload settings: `wpa_passphrase` turns the password (given on its stdin) into the WPA2 key, and `/run/persist/u2ac-home.conf` gets `SSID=`, `PMK=` (that key, never the password) and `URL=http://A.B.C.D:PORT[/path]`, then `u2ac-aa persist`. Port 9091 when none is given. |
+| `home-off` | | Removes the home upload settings and what it learned (`u2ac-home.freq`, `u2ac-home.sent`), then `u2ac-aa persist`. |
+| `home-now` | | `u2ac-aa home-now`: an upload now. The hotspot stops for the few seconds Wi-Fi is a client of the home network. |
+| `aa-now` | | `u2ac-aa aa-now`. |
+| `reboot` | | `u2ac-aa persist`, then `reboot` 1 s after the reply. |
+| `recovery` | | Same with `reboot-recovery` (only if it is on PATH). |
+
+Input rules, checked again on the server: Wi-Fi name 1 to 32 printable ASCII characters, password 8 to 63,
+neither containing `"` or `\`; Bluetooth name 1 to 32 of `A-Z a-z 0-9 space _ -`; addresses
+`XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX` in upper-case hex. The Pushgateway address: an IPv4 address, port 1 to 65535, path of
+`A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ ~ / -` without `..` (the dongle has no DNS). A body holding anything other than form-urlencoded characters is
+refused before decoding; decoded values outside printable ASCII are refused. User input is never
+`eval`ed or put in a `sed`/`awk` program: it is written with `printf '%s'` or passed through awk
+`ENVIRON`. One change runs at a time (`flock` on `/run/u2ac-web/action.lock`).
+
+## The Wi-Fi override file
+
+`/run/persist/u2ac-wifi.conf` (mode 0600, saved in the persistent store), exactly two lines:
+
+```
+SSID=<name>
+PSK=<password>
+```
+
+Contract for the reader (`u2ac-aa`, before it starts `hostapd`):
+
+- Read the values literally, the rest of the line after the first `=`. **Never source the file** (`.`):
+  the values may hold `$`, backticks, `;` and spaces.
+- Both keys are always written together; `PSK` is the WPA2 passphrase.
+- The same values are in config.toml, so aa-proxy-rs tells the phone the credentials the AP uses.
+  If the AP ignores the override, the phone is sent a password the AP does not accept.
+
+`ap_up` in `/usr/sbin/u2ac-aa` reads it this way (length checks included) before it starts `hostapd`.
+
+## Security
+
+The page is reachable only on the dongle's WPA2 AP and the USB link. On top of that, every POST to
+`cgi-bin/action` needs an access code:
+
+- 32 hex characters in `/run/persist/u2ac-webtoken` (0600), created by the first `GET cgi-bin/token`
+  when the file does not exist (atomically, so only one visitor gets it) and saved to flash at once
+  (`u2ac-aa persist`: a code lost at ignition-off would reopen the window below on the next boot).
+- `cgi-bin/token` returns the code to clients on the USB link (`REMOTE_ADDR` in 192.168.50.0/24), once
+  after `touch /run/u2ac-web/reveal-once` (over ssh), and to the request that created it, but on the
+  hotspot only once its password is no longer the vendor default (12345678: anyone in range can join).
+  Everyone else gets `null` and types the code in; the page keeps it in `localStorage`.
+- Mutations are POST only and also need `confirm=yes` (the page asks first). A cross-site form cannot
+  know the code, so it cannot make changes.
+- To change the code: `rm /run/persist/u2ac-webtoken` and open the page (or write 32 hex characters to it).
+
+## Testing on a host
+
+The scripts take `FAKE_ROOT` (prefix for every file path) and `FAKE_PATH` (directories put first on
+PATH, for stubs of `iw`, `btmgmt`, `u2ac-aa`, `persist`, `reboot`, `dumpleases`). With Docker:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm -p 127.0.0.1:18080:80 -v "$PWD":/www:ro -v <fake-root>:/fake -v <stubs>:/stubs:ro \
+    -e FAKE_ROOT=/fake -e FAKE_PATH=/stubs busybox:1.37 httpd -f -p 80 -h /www
+```
+
+The state shown is a heuristic: `streaming` means aa-proxy-rs is running, a Wi-Fi station is
+associated, and the newest session event in the last 120 log lines is `first video frame` (not
+followed by `session time:`, `closing session`, `disconnected phone`, `Terminated single session`,
+`ByeBye`, `session error` or `connection reset`).
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/_lib.sh b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/_lib.sh
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..65ebc78
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/_lib.sh
@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+# u2ac web UI: helpers shared by the CGI scripts (sourced, never executed; mode 0644 so httpd will not
+# run it). POSIX sh / BusyBox ash + BusyBox applets only. User input is never eval'd, never used in a
+# sed/awk program or a regex: it reaches files only through printf '%s' and awk ENVIRON[].
+#
+# FAKE_ROOT (host self-test only, unset on the unit): prefix for every file path, so the scripts can run
+# against a fake /proc, /sys, /run, /etc and /var tree. Commands (iw, btmgmt, u2ac-aa, persist, reboot,
+# dumpleases) are found on PATH, so a test puts stubs first on PATH.
+R=${FAKE_ROOT:-}
+P=$R/run/persist
+WEB=$R/run/u2ac-web
+TOKEN=$P/u2ac-webtoken
+WIFI_OVR=$P/u2ac-wifi.conf
+HOMECONF=$P/u2ac-home.conf
+AACFG=$R/etc/aa-proxy-rs/config.toml
+BTLIB=$R/var/lib/bluetooth
+HAPCONF=$R/usr/share/u2ac/hostapd.conf
+LEASES=$R/run/udhcpd-wlan.leases
+SVCLOG=$R/run/log/u2ac-aa.log
+HAPLOG=$R/run/log/hostapd.log
+BTLOG=$R/run/log/bluetoothd.log
+AALOG=$R/var/log/aa-proxy-rs.log
+[ -s "$AALOG" ] || [ ! -s "$R/run/log/aa-proxy-rs.console" ] || AALOG=$R/run/log/aa-proxy-rs.console
+WEBLOG=$R/run/log/u2ac-web.log
+
+PATH=/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin${PATH:+:$PATH}
+[ -n "${FAKE_PATH:-}" ] && PATH=$FAKE_PATH:$PATH
+export PATH
+mkdir -p "$WEB" 2>/dev/null
+
+TO=; command -v timeout > /dev/null 2>&1 && TO="timeout 4"
+
+# btm ARGS: btmgmt with an open, empty FIFO as stdin. BlueZ 5.87's btmgmt reads a non-tty stdin as a command
+# script and quits at its EOF before the kernel's reply (a POST CGI's stdin is the drained body: an unpair
+# could be dropped); the same fix as u2ac-aa's bt_up. fd 9 (callers' locks) is not passed on.
+btm() {
+    _bf=$WEB/btmgmt.$$
+    rm -f "$_bf"
+    if mkfifo "$_bf" 2> /dev/null && exec 7<> "$_bf"; then
+        rm -f "$_bf"; $TO btmgmt "$@" 9>&- <&7; _br=$?; exec 7<&-
+    else
+        rm -f "$_bf"; $TO btmgmt "$@" 9>&- < /dev/null; _br=$?
+    fi
+    return $_br
+}
+
+# awk functions: rep (literal replace, no regex/backslash surprises), jesc (JSON string body)
+AWKLIB='
+function rep(s, f, t,   o, i) { o = ""; while ((i = index(s, f)) > 0) { o = o substr(s, 1, i - 1) t; s = substr(s, i + length(f)) } return o s }
+function jesc(s) { s = rep(s, "\\", "\\\\"); s = rep(s, "\"", "\\\""); gsub(/\t/, " ", s); gsub(/[\001-\037\177]/, "", s); return s }
+function js(s) { return "\"" jesc(s) "\"" }
+function noansi(s) { gsub(/\033\[[0-9;?]*[A-Za-z]/, "", s); gsub(/\033[()][A-Z0-9]/, "", s); return s }
+'
+
+hdr() { printf 'Content-Type: application/json\r\nCache-Control: no-store\r\n\r\n'; }
+
+# jstr STRING: STRING as a JSON string literal (quotes included)
+jstr() { printf '%s' "$1" | awk "$AWKLIB"'BEGIN { ORS = ""; o = "" } { o = o (NR > 1 ? "\\n" : "") jesc($0) } END { print "\"" o "\"" }'; }
+
+# fail MESSAGE [CODE]: MESSAGE and CODE are fixed text from these scripts, never user input
+fail() { hdr; printf '{"ok":false,"error":%s,"code":"%s"}\n' "$(jstr "$1")" "${2:-error}"; exit 0; }
+
+now() { _up=; { read -r _up _ < "$R/proc/uptime"; } 2> /dev/null; NOW=${_up%%.*}; case $NOW in '' | *[!0-9]*) NOW=0 ;; esac; }
+
+# cache NAME TTL CMD...: refresh $WEB/NAME from CMD when older than TTL seconds (stamp = uptime, 1st line)
+cache() {
+    _cf=$WEB/$1 _ttl=$2; shift 2
+    if [ -s "$_cf" ]; then
+        { read -r _ _cts < "$_cf"; } 2> /dev/null
+        case $_cts in '' | *[!0-9]*) _cts=-99999 ;; esac
+        [ $((NOW - _cts)) -lt "$_ttl" ] && [ "$_cts" -le "$NOW" ] && return 0
+    fi
+    { echo "T $NOW"; "$@" 2> /dev/null; } > "$_cf.$$" && mv -f "$_cf.$$" "$_cf"
+}
+
+# query/body fields. qfield NAME -> $FV from QUERY_STRING (raw), field NAME -> $FV from the POST body (raw)
+qfield() { _q="&${QUERY_STRING:-}"; case $_q in *"&$1="*) FV=${_q#*"&$1="}; FV=${FV%%&*} ;; *) FV=; return 1 ;; esac; }
+field() { case "&$BODY" in *"&$1="*) FV="&$BODY"; FV=${FV#*"&$1="}; FV=${FV%%&*} ;; *) FV=; return 1 ;; esac; }
+
+read_body() {
+    [ "${REQUEST_METHOD:-}" = POST ] || fail "use POST" method
+    _n=${CONTENT_LENGTH:-0}
+    case $_n in '' | *[!0-9]*) _n=0 ;; esac
+    [ "$_n" -gt 4096 ] && fail "request too large" size
+    BODY=
+    [ "$_n" -gt 0 ] && BODY=$(head -c "$_n")
+    # the body itself is form-urlencoded: anything else in it is refused before any decoding
+    case $BODY in *[!A-Za-z0-9%+=\&._~*-]*) fail "malformed request" input ;; esac
+}
+
+# urldec RAW: form-urldecode; fails (no output) if the result would hold anything outside printable ASCII
+urldec() {
+    V=$1 awk 'BEGIN { s = ENVIRON["V"]; o = ""; h = "0123456789abcdef"; L = length(s)
+        for (i = 1; i <= L; i++) {
+            c = substr(s, i, 1)
+            if (c == "+") c = " "
+            else if (c == "%") {
+                a = index(h, tolower(substr(s, i + 1, 1))) - 1; b = index(h, tolower(substr(s, i + 2, 1))) - 1
+                if (a < 0 || b < 0) exit 1
+                n = a * 16 + b; if (n < 32 || n > 126) exit 1
+                c = sprintf("%c", n); i += 2
+            } else if (c < " " || c > "~") exit 1
+            o = o c
+        }
+        printf "%s", o }'
+}
+
+# validators (input already printable ASCII after urldec)
+valid_ssid() { [ ${#1} -ge 1 ] && [ ${#1} -le 32 ] && case $1 in *[\"\\]*) false ;; *) true ;; esac; }
+valid_psk() { [ ${#1} -ge 8 ] && [ ${#1} -le 63 ] && case $1 in *[\"\\]*) false ;; *) true ;; esac; }
+valid_alias() { [ ${#1} -ge 1 ] && [ ${#1} -le 32 ] && case $1 in *[!A-Za-z0-9\ _-]*) false ;; *) true ;; esac; }
+valid_mac() { case $1 in [0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]) true ;; *) false ;; esac; }
+
+# token: 32 hex chars in $P/u2ac-webtoken (0600), made on first use
+token_read() { TOK=; [ -s "$TOKEN" ] && read -r TOK < "$TOKEN"; case $TOK in *[!0-9a-f]* | '') TOK= ;; esac; }
+token_new() {
+    _t=$(tr -d '-' < /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid 2> /dev/null)
+    case $_t in ???????????????????????????????? ) ;; *) _t=$(od -An -N16 -tx1 /dev/urandom | tr -d ' \n') ;; esac
+    mkdir -p "$P" || return 1
+    # noclobber = O_EXCL: of two first visitors only one creates (and is shown) the token
+    (umask 077; set -C; printf '%s\n' "$_t" > "$TOKEN") 2> /dev/null
+}
+need_token() {
+    token_read
+    [ -n "$TOK" ] || fail "no access code exists yet: open the dashboard once to create it" token
+    field token || fail "this browser has no access code" token
+    [ "$FV" = "$TOK" ] || fail "wrong access code" token
+}
+# wireless interface: the first one with a phy80211 link in sysfs (never assumed), wlan0 if none is up yet
+wif() {
+    WIF=
+    for _w in "$R"/sys/class/net/*; do
+        [ -e "$_w/phy80211" ] && { WIF=${_w##*/}; break; }
+    done
+    : "${WIF:=wlan0}"
+}
+# REMOTE_ADDR: "a.b.c.d" on an IPv4 listener, "[::ffff:a.b.c.d]" on a dual-stack one
+from_usb() { _ra=${REMOTE_ADDR:-}; _ra=${_ra#[}; _ra=${_ra%]}; _ra=${_ra#::ffff:}; case $_ra in 192.168.50.*) true ;; *) false ;; esac; }
+
+weblog() { now; printf '%s web[%s]: %s\n' "$NOW" "${REMOTE_ADDR:-?}" "$*" >> "$WEBLOG" 2> /dev/null; }
+
+# tomlget KEY FILE: value of the first two-space-indented `KEY = "..."` line
+tomlget() {
+    K=$1 awk 'index($0, "  " ENVIRON["K"] " = \"") == 1 { s = substr($0, length(ENVIRON["K"]) + 7); i = index(s, "\""); while (i > 0 && substr(s, i - 1, 1) == "\\") { j = index(substr(s, i + 1), "\""); i = j ? i + j : 0 } print (i ? substr(s, 1, i - 1) : s); exit }' "$2" 2> /dev/null
+}
+# ovrget KEY: SSID or PSK from the override file (read literally, never sourced)
+ovrget() { K=$1 awk 'index($0, ENVIRON["K"] "=") == 1 { print substr($0, length(ENVIRON["K"]) + 2); exit }' "$WIFI_OVR" 2> /dev/null; }
+# hget KEY: SSID, PMK or URL from the home upload settings (u2ac-home), read the same way
+hget() { K=$1 awk 'index($0, ENVIRON["K"] "=") == 1 { print substr($0, length(ENVIRON["K"]) + 2); exit }' "$HOMECONF" 2> /dev/null; }
+# home_url TEXT: a Pushgateway address as http://A.B.C.D:PORT[/path] (port 9091 when none is given); fails on
+# anything else (an IPv4 address only: the dongle has no DNS)
+home_url() {
+    _u=${1#http://}; _hp=${_u%%/*}; _pa=
+    case $_u in */*) _pa=/${_u#*/} ;; esac
+    _pa=${_pa%/}; _h=${_hp%:*}; _po=${_hp##*:}
+    [ "$_h" = "$_hp" ] && _po=9091
+    case $_h in '' | *[!0-9.]*) return 1 ;; esac
+    H=$_h awk 'BEGIN { n = split(ENVIRON["H"], a, "."); if (n != 4) exit 1
+        for (i = 1; i <= 4; i++) if (a[i] == "" || length(a[i]) > 3 || a[i] + 0 > 255) exit 1 }' || return 1
+    case $_po in '' | *[!0-9]*) return 1 ;; esac
+    [ ${#_po} -le 5 ] && [ "$_po" -ge 1 ] && [ "$_po" -le 65535 ] || return 1
+    case $_pa in *[!A-Za-z0-9._~/-]* | *..*) return 1 ;; esac
+    printf 'http://%s:%s%s' "$_h" "$_po" "$_pa"
+}
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/about b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/about
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..b88e822
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/about
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+# GET /cgi-bin/about -> versions (cached for the boot: they cannot change while it runs) + CPU
+# frequency residency (cpufreq stats/time_in_state, live).
+_d=${0%/*}; [ "$_d" = "$0" ] && _d=.
+. "$_d/_lib.sh"
+
+V=$WEB/versions
+if [ ! -s "$V" ]; then
+    # ver NAME CMD...: first line of CMD's output, only if CMD exists (no "not found" text in the UI)
+    ver() { _n=$1; shift; command -v "$1" > /dev/null 2>&1 || return 0; echo "$_n=$($TO "$@" < /dev/null 2>&1 | grep -m 1 .)"; }
+    {
+        echo "kernel=$(uname -r 2> /dev/null) $(uname -v 2> /dev/null)"
+        echo "build=$(head -n 1 "$R/etc/baseline-release" 2> /dev/null)"
+        echo "board=$(sed -n 's/^BOARD_NAME="\{0,1\}\([^"]*\)"\{0,1\}$/\1/p' "$R/etc/baseline/board.env" 2> /dev/null | head -n 1)"
+        ver aa-proxy-rs aa-proxy-rs --version
+        _b=/usr/libexec/bluetooth/bluetoothd; [ -x "$_b" ] || _b=bluetoothd
+        ver bluez "$_b" --version
+        ver hostapd hostapd -v
+        ver iw iw --version
+        echo "busybox=$(busybox 2>&1 | head -n 1 | sed 's/ multi-call binary.*//')"
+        echo "machine=$(uname -m 2> /dev/null)"
+    } > "$V.$$" && mv -f "$V.$$" "$V"
+fi
+
+hdr
+awk -v st="$R/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/stats/time_in_state" -v gov="$R/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpufreq/scaling_governor" "$AWKLIB"'
+BEGIN { printf "{\"ok\":true,\"versions\":{" }
+{ i = index($0, "="); if (!i) next; printf "%s%s:%s", (n++ ? "," : ""), js(substr($0, 1, i - 1)), js(substr($0, i + 1)) }
+END {
+    printf "},\"cpu\":{\"governor\":"; g = ""; getline g < gov; printf "%s,\"time_in_state\":[", js(g)
+    k = 0; while ((getline l < st) > 0) { split(l, a, " "); if (a[1] ~ /^[0-9]+$/) printf "%s{\"khz\":%d,\"ticks\":%d}", (k++ ? "," : ""), a[1], a[2] }
+    printf "]}}\n"
+}' "$V"
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/action b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/action
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..4984259
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/action
@@ -0,0 +1,239 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+# POST /cgi-bin/action (application/x-www-form-urlencoded), fields:
+#   token=<access code>  confirm=yes  action=<one of below> [+ its fields]
+#   wifi      ssid= psk= alias=   (each optional; empty = keep. SSID 1-32 printable ASCII without " or \,
+#                                  password 8-63 printable ASCII without " or \, Bluetooth name 1-32 [A-Za-z0-9 _-])
+#   forget    dev=<AA:BB:CC:DD:EE:FF>|all
+#   mode      to=auto|maintenance|aa
+#   home      ssid= psk= url=     (home upload: the home Wi-Fi and a Pushgateway's IPv4 address[:port][/path];
+#                                  psk may stay empty when the name is unchanged; only the derived key is kept)
+#   home-off | home-now
+#   aa-now | reboot | recovery
+# -> {"ok":true,"msg":"...","reboot":bool} or {"ok":false,"error":"...","code":"token|input|..."}
+_d=${0%/*}; [ "$_d" = "$0" ] && _d=.
+. "$_d/_lib.sh"
+
+read_body
+need_token
+field confirm; [ "$FV" = yes ] || fail "not confirmed" confirm
+field action; ACT=$FV
+
+# one change at a time (from this UI; the service's 30 s saver is not part of this lock)
+exec 9> "$WEB/action.lock"
+command -v flock > /dev/null 2>&1 && { flock -n 9 || fail "another change is still running: try again in a moment" busy; }
+
+ok() { # ok MESSAGE [REBOOT]: fixed text from this script, plus the output of our own commands
+    hdr; printf '{"ok":true,"msg":%s,"reboot":%s}\n' "$(jstr "$1")" "${2:-false}"; exit 0
+}
+run() { # run CMD...: CMD's output (stdin /dev/null) into $OUT, logged
+    "$@" 9>&- < /dev/null > "$WEB/out.$$" 2>&1; _rc=$?
+    OUT=$(cat "$WEB/out.$$" 2> /dev/null); rm -f "$WEB/out.$$"
+    printf '%s\n' "$OUT" | sed "s/^/  $1: /" >> "$WEBLOG" 2> /dev/null
+    return $_rc
+}
+detach() { # detach CMD...: start CMD after this response is out, in its own session
+    if command -v setsid > /dev/null 2>&1; then
+        setsid sh -c 'sleep 1; exec "$@"' u2ac-web "$@" 9>&- < /dev/null > /dev/null 2>&1 &
+    else
+        sh -c 'sleep 1; exec "$@"' u2ac-web "$@" 9>&- < /dev/null > /dev/null 2>&1 &
+    fi
+}
+
+case $ACT in
+wifi)
+    field ssid; NS=; [ -n "$FV" ] && { NS=$(urldec "$FV") || fail "the Wi-Fi name has a character that is not allowed" input; }
+    field psk; NP=; [ -n "$FV" ] && { NP=$(urldec "$FV") || fail "the password has a character that is not allowed" input; }
+    field alias; NA=; [ -n "$FV" ] && { NA=$(urldec "$FV") || fail "the Bluetooth name has a character that is not allowed" input; }
+    [ -n "$NS$NP$NA" ] || fail "nothing to change" input
+    [ -z "$NS" ] || valid_ssid "$NS" || fail "Wi-Fi name: 1 to 32 characters, no \" or \\" input
+    [ -z "$NP" ] || valid_psk "$NP" || fail "password: 8 to 63 characters, no \" or \\" input
+    [ -z "$NA" ] || valid_alias "$NA" || fail "Bluetooth name: 1 to 32 letters, digits, spaces, _ or -" input
+    [ -s "$AACFG" ] || fail "no aa-proxy-rs config at /etc/aa-proxy-rs/config.toml" config
+    # current values fill what was left empty, so config.toml and the override always agree
+    CS=$(tomlget ssid "$AACFG"); CP=$(tomlget wpa_passphrase "$AACFG")
+    [ -s "$WIFI_OVR" ] && { _o=$(ovrget SSID); [ -n "$_o" ] && CS=$_o; _o=$(ovrget PSK); [ -n "$_o" ] && CP=$_o; }
+    : "${NS:=$CS}" "${NP:=$CP}"
+    valid_ssid "$NS" && valid_psk "$NP" || fail "the current Wi-Fi name or password is not valid: set both" input
+    # config.toml: replace the first `  ssid = `, `  wpa_passphrase = ` and (if given) `  btalias = ` lines
+    _new=$AACFG.web.$$
+    NS=$NS NP=$NP NA=$NA awk '
+        !s && index($0, "  ssid = \"") == 1 { print "  ssid = \"" ENVIRON["NS"] "\""; s = 1; next }
+        !p && index($0, "  wpa_passphrase = \"") == 1 { print "  wpa_passphrase = \"" ENVIRON["NP"] "\""; p = 1; next }
+        !a && ENVIRON["NA"] != "" && index($0, "  btalias = \"") == 1 { print "  btalias = \"" ENVIRON["NA"] "\""; a = 1; next }
+        { print }
+        END { if (!s || !p || (ENVIRON["NA"] != "" && !a)) exit 3 }' "$AACFG" > "$_new" \
+        || { rm -f "$_new"; fail "config.toml has no ssid / wpa_passphrase / btalias line to change" config; }
+    CFGCH=0
+    cmp -s "$_new" "$AACFG" || { mv -f "$_new" "$AACFG" && CFGCH=1; } || fail "could not write config.toml" config
+    rm -f "$_new"
+    # the override the service reads at boot (literal KEY=value lines, never sourced)
+    mkdir -p "$P"
+    _ov=$WEB/wifi.$$ OVRCH=0
+    (umask 077; printf 'SSID=%s\nPSK=%s\n' "$NS" "$NP" > "$_ov") || fail "could not write the Wi-Fi override" persist
+    cmp -s "$_ov" "$WIFI_OVR" 2> /dev/null || OVRCH=1
+    if [ $OVRCH = 1 ]; then mv -f "$_ov" "$WIFI_OVR" || fail "could not write /run/persist/u2ac-wifi.conf" persist; fi
+    rm -f "$_ov"
+    [ $CFGCH = 0 ] && [ $OVRCH = 0 ] && ok "Nothing changed: these are the current settings."
+    weblog "wifi/bt settings changed (ssid ${#NS} chars, alias ${NA:+set})"
+    # u2ac-aa persist writes the store when anything in /run/persist (override included) or config.toml changed
+    run u2ac-aa persist || fail "saved for this boot, but writing the persistent store failed (see the Service log)" persist
+    : > "$WEB/pending-reboot"
+    ok "Saved. Reboot the dongle to use the new settings, then reconnect your phone to the new Wi-Fi name." true
+    ;;
+forget)
+    field dev; D=$FV
+    [ "$D" = all ] || { D=$(urldec "$D") && valid_mac "$D"; } || fail "not a Bluetooth address" input
+    C=0
+    for _x in "$BTLIB"/*/[0-9A-F][0-9A-F]:??:??:??:??:??; do
+        [ -d "$_x" ] || continue
+        _dev=${_x##*/} _ad=${_x%/*}
+        valid_mac "$_dev" || continue
+        [ "$D" = all ] || [ "$D" = "$_dev" ] || continue
+        btm -i hci0 unpair "$_dev" > /dev/null 2>&1
+        rm -rf "$_x" "$_ad/cache/$_dev"
+        C=$((C + 1))
+    done
+    [ $C = 0 ] && fail "no such paired phone" input
+    # aa-proxy-rs's own list of phones it dials after a reboot (one address per line): drop them there too
+    KD=$R/etc/aa-proxy-rs/known_devices
+    if [ -f "$KD" ]; then
+        if [ "$D" = all ]; then : > "$KD"
+        else D=$D awk '{ l = $0; gsub(/[ \t\r]/, "", l); if (toupper(l) != ENVIRON["D"]) print }' "$KD" > "$KD.web" \
+            && mv -f "$KD.web" "$KD"; fi
+    fi
+    weblog "forgot $C paired device(s)"
+    run u2ac-aa persist || fail "forgotten for this boot, but writing the persistent store failed" persist
+    if [ $C = 1 ]; then ok "Forgot 1 phone. Remove the dongle from the phone's Bluetooth list too."
+    else ok "Forgot $C phones. Remove the dongle from each phone's Bluetooth list too."; fi
+    ;;
+mode)
+    field to
+    case $FV in
+        auto) A=off M="Automatic: Android Auto in the car, maintenance when a computer is on USB." ;;
+        maintenance) A=on M="Maintenance: USB stays a network link to the computer, Android Auto does not start." ;;
+        aa) A=aa M="Android Auto always, even with a computer on USB." ;;
+        *) fail "unknown mode" input ;;
+    esac
+    run u2ac-aa dev "$A" || fail "u2ac-aa dev $A failed" service
+    weblog "mode -> $FV"
+    ok "$M Applies from the next boot." true
+    ;;
+width)
+    # the hotspot's channel width from the next boot: /run/persist/u2ac-wifi-80 (u2ac-aa ap_up uses the 80 MHz
+    # config only when the flag exists AND the Wi-Fi firmware offers VHT80 on channel 36)
+    field to
+    case $FV in
+        40) rm -f "$P/u2ac-wifi-80" || fail "could not change the setting" persist
+            M="Wi-Fi at 40 MHz (the default)." ;;
+        80) (umask 077; : > "$P/u2ac-wifi-80") || fail "could not change the setting" persist
+            M="Wi-Fi at 80 MHz." ;;
+        *) fail "unknown width" input ;;
+    esac
+    run u2ac-aa persist || fail "set for this boot, but writing the persistent store failed" persist
+    : > "$WEB/pending-reboot"
+    weblog "wifi width -> $FV MHz"
+    ok "$M It applies after a reboot." true
+    ;;
+opt)
+    # the dongle's other switches (persist flags read at boot or by the service):
+    # one key per request, only the keys and values listed here, anything else is refused
+    field key; K=$FV
+    field value; V=$FV
+    optflag() { # optflag FILE set|clear
+        if [ "$2" = set ]; then (umask 077; : > "$P/$1"); else rm -f "$P/$1"; fi \
+            || fail "could not change the setting" persist
+    }
+    WHEN=reboot
+    case $K:$V in
+        guard:on) optflag u2ac-hfp-guard-off clear; M="Hands-free guard on." ;;
+        guard:off) optflag u2ac-hfp-guard-off set; M="Hands-free guard off." ;;
+        flightlog:on) optflag u2ac-flightlog-off clear; M="Flight recorder on."; WHEN=now ;;
+        flightlog:off) optflag u2ac-flightlog-off set; M="Flight recorder off."; WHEN=now ;;
+        sleep:on) optflag u2ac-sleep-off clear; M="Sleep when the car is off: on."; WHEN=now ;;
+        sleep:off) optflag u2ac-sleep-off set; M="Sleep when the car is off: off."; WHEN=now ;;
+        # on: lit again at once in its last colour (steady); its next state change restores the blink pattern
+        led:on) optflag u2ac-led-off clear; echo 255 > "$R/sys/class/leds/rgb:status/brightness" 2> /dev/null
+            M="Status light on."; WHEN=now ;;
+        led:off) optflag u2ac-led-off set; echo 0 > "$R/sys/class/leds/rgb:status/brightness" 2> /dev/null
+            M="Status light off."; WHEN=now ;;
+        btbaud:fast) optflag u2ac-bt-slowbaud clear; M="Bluetooth firmware download at 3 Mbaud (the default)." ;;
+        btbaud:slow) optflag u2ac-bt-slowbaud set; M="Bluetooth firmware download at 115200 baud." ;;
+        fastflash:on) optflag u2ac-qspi-normal clear; M="Fast flash reads at boot: on." ;;
+        fastflash:off) optflag u2ac-qspi-normal set; M="Fast flash reads at boot: off." ;;
+        btpatch:stock) optflag u2ac-bt-0092 clear; M="Stock Bluetooth patch (0082, the default)." ;;
+        btpatch:0092) optflag u2ac-bt-0092 set; M="Newer Bluetooth patch (0092)." ;;
+        usbchunk:16384) optflag u2ac-ffs-chunk clear; M="USB transfers of 16384 bytes (the default)." ;;
+        usbchunk:512 | usbchunk:1024 | usbchunk:2048 | usbchunk:4096 | usbchunk:8192)
+            (umask 077; printf '%s\n' "$V" > "$P/u2ac-ffs-chunk") || fail "could not change the setting" persist
+            M="USB transfers of $V bytes." ;;
+        *) fail "unknown option or value" input ;;
+    esac
+    run u2ac-aa persist || fail "set for this boot, but writing the persistent store failed" persist
+    weblog "option $K -> $V"
+    [ $WHEN = now ] && ok "$M"
+    : > "$WEB/pending-reboot"
+    ok "$M It applies after a reboot." true
+    ;;
+home)
+    # the home upload (u2ac-home). The password is turned into the WPA2 key at once (wpa_passphrase, the key
+    # depends on the name too) and is never written anywhere; it reaches wpa_passphrase on stdin, not argv
+    field ssid; NS=; [ -n "$FV" ] && { NS=$(urldec "$FV") || fail "the home Wi-Fi name has a character that is not allowed" input; }
+    field psk; NP=; [ -n "$FV" ] && { NP=$(urldec "$FV") || fail "the password has a character that is not allowed" input; }
+    field url; NU=; [ -n "$FV" ] && { NU=$(urldec "$FV") || fail "the server address has a character that is not allowed" input; }
+    valid_ssid "$NS" || fail "home Wi-Fi name: 1 to 32 characters, no \" or \\" input
+    [ -z "$NP" ] || valid_psk "$NP" || fail "home Wi-Fi password: 8 to 63 characters, no \" or \\" input
+    NU=$(home_url "$NU") || fail "server: an IPv4 address with an optional port and path, like 192.168.1.10:9091" input
+    OS=$(hget SSID); OK=$(hget PMK)
+    if [ -n "$NP" ]; then
+        K=$(printf '%s\n' "$NP" | wpa_passphrase "$NS" 2> /dev/null \
+            | awk '$1 ~ /^psk=[0-9a-f]+$/ && length($1) == 68 { print substr($1, 5); exit }')
+        [ ${#K} = 64 ] || fail "could not derive the Wi-Fi key (wpa_passphrase)" service
+    elif [ "$NS" = "$OS" ] && [ ${#OK} = 64 ]; then K=$OK
+    else fail "enter the home Wi-Fi password too (the key depends on the name)" input; fi
+    mkdir -p "$P"
+    _hc=$WEB/home.$$
+    (umask 077; printf 'SSID=%s\nPMK=%s\nURL=%s\n' "$NS" "$K" "$NU" > "$_hc") || fail "could not write the settings" persist
+    if cmp -s "$_hc" "$HOMECONF" 2> /dev/null; then rm -f "$_hc"; ok "Nothing changed: these are the current settings."; fi
+    mv -f "$_hc" "$HOMECONF" || { rm -f "$_hc"; fail "could not write /run/persist/u2ac-home.conf" persist; }
+    # another network: its channel is learned again
+    [ "$NS" = "$OS" ] || rm -f "$P/u2ac-home.freq"
+    weblog "home upload set (ssid ${#NS} chars)"
+    run u2ac-aa persist || fail "saved for this boot, but writing the persistent store failed (see the Service log)" persist
+    ok "Saved. The dongle sends its drive logs when it starts near your home network. Use Upload now to try it."
+    ;;
+home-off)
+    rm -f "$HOMECONF" "$P/u2ac-home.freq" "$P/u2ac-home.sent" || fail "could not change the setting" persist
+    weblog "home upload off"
+    run u2ac-aa persist || fail "turned off for this boot, but writing the persistent store failed" persist
+    ok "Home upload off. The dongle forgot the home network."
+    ;;
+home-now)
+    [ -s "$HOMECONF" ] || fail "the home upload is not set up" input
+    run ${TO:+timeout 60} u2ac-aa home-now; _rc=$?
+    weblog "home upload by hand: rc $_rc"
+    _m=$(printf '%s\n' "$OUT" | tail -n 1)
+    [ $_rc = 0 ] && ok "Upload: $_m."
+    fail "upload: ${_m:-no answer}" upload
+    ;;
+aa-now)
+    run u2ac-aa aa-now || fail "could not start Android Auto" service
+    weblog "aa-now"
+    case $OUT in *already*) ok "Android Auto is already running." ;; esac
+    ok "Android Auto is starting. A network link to a computer on USB goes away now."
+    ;;
+reboot)
+    run u2ac-aa persist
+    weblog "reboot"
+    detach reboot
+    ok "Rebooting. This page reconnects by itself in about 40 seconds." false
+    ;;
+recovery)
+    command -v reboot-recovery > /dev/null 2>&1 || fail "this build has no reboot-recovery" input
+    run u2ac-aa persist
+    weblog "reboot-recovery"
+    detach reboot-recovery
+    ok "Rebooting into recovery. This page will not answer until the normal system is back." false
+    ;;
+*) fail "unknown action" input ;;
+esac
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/logs b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/logs
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..1b8581f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/logs
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+# GET /cgi-bin/logs?src=aa|svc|hostapd|bt|web|dmesg&n=200 -> {"ok","src","file","lines":[...]}
+# The last n lines (20..500, default 200), ANSI colour codes and control characters stripped.
+_d=${0%/*}; [ "$_d" = "$0" ] && _d=.
+. "$_d/_lib.sh"
+
+qfield src; SRC=$FV
+qfield n; N=$FV
+case $N in '' | *[!0-9]*) N=200 ;; esac
+[ "$N" -lt 20 ] && N=20
+[ "$N" -gt 500 ] && N=500
+
+case $SRC in
+    svc) F=$SVCLOG ;;
+    hostapd) F=$HAPLOG ;;
+    bt) F=$BTLOG ;;
+    web) F=$WEBLOG ;;
+    dmesg) F=dmesg ;;
+    flight) F=flight ;;
+    *) SRC=aa F=$AALOG ;;
+esac
+
+hdr
+{
+    if [ "$SRC" = dmesg ]; then dmesg 2> /dev/null | tail -n "$N"
+    elif [ "$SRC" = flight ]; then
+        # the list, then the newest car run from its top (status, service log, then aa-proxy-rs's)
+        { u2ac-aa flightlog; echo; u2ac-aa flightlog last; } 2> /dev/null | head -n "$N"
+    else tail -n "$N" "$F" 2> /dev/null; fi
+} | awk -v src="$SRC" -v f="${F#"$R"}" "$AWKLIB"'
+BEGIN { printf "{\"ok\":true,\"src\":\"%s\",\"file\":%s,\"lines\":[", src, js(f) }
+{ l = noansi($0); sub(/\r$/, "", l); sub(/^ +/, "", l); if (length(l) > 600) l = substr(l, 1, 600) "..."; printf "%s%s", (NR > 1 ? "," : ""), js(l) }
+END { print "]}" }'
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/metrics b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/metrics
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..51ed059
--- /dev/null
+++ b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/metrics
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
+# GET /cgi-bin/metrics: the dongle's health for Prometheus (u2ac-metrics). Read-only and free of MAC
+# addresses, names and keys, so no token: a scraper sends no cookie.
+_d=${0%/*}; [ "$_d" = "$0" ] && _d=.
+. "$_d/_lib.sh"
+printf 'Content-Type: text/plain; version=0.0.4; charset=utf-8\r\nCache-Control: no-store\r\n\r\n'
+exec u2ac-metrics
diff --git a/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/settings b/baseline/arm-imx6ul-u2ac/rootfs/usr/share/u2ac/www/cgi-bin/settings
